{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cfgr8Vr215ri32WxwxBqZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is well-structured and idiomatic for this package:\n\n- **Right unit / single source of truth.** The new `OwnerAddress.normalize` mirrors the existing `OwnerHousehold` \"centralize the rule so sites can't disagree\" pattern, and its Javadoc explicitly names the three consumers (`ValidateOwnerFields` stores/rejects, `OwnerHousehold` compares). Address normalization genuinely differs from last-name normalization (upper-case + abbreviation expansion vs. lower-case), so giving address its own class rather than overloading `OwnerHousehold.normalize` is the correct split, not a forced one.\n\n- **No catch-all growth.** `ValidateOwnerFields` gains only the field-specific normalize-then-check-then-write-back, with a clear comment on why it writes the canonical value back; `OwnerHousehold` delegates to `OwnerAddress.normalize` rather than inlining, keeping each class focused.\n\n- **Coherent delegation.** `OwnerHousehold.matches`/`deriveId` normalizing both sides themselves (rather than assuming `ValidateOwnerFields` already mutated the request) is the right call for a class that advertises itself as the household source of truth — it stays self-contained and the re-normalization is idempotent.\n\n- **Docs kept in sync.** `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`, `OwnerHousehold`, and the repurposed `OwnerHousehold.normalize` comment (\"last-name comparison form\") were all updated, so a maintainer isn't left with stale descriptions.\n\nMinor, non-blocking: `OwnerHousehold.normalize` and `OwnerAddress.normalize` both re-implement trim + whitespace-collapse. The shared slice is tiny and the two policies are genuinely distinct, so extracting a common whitespace primitive would be over-engineering here rather than a cleanup — not worth requesting a change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11819,"cache_read_input_tokens":11894,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11819},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7858513f-91bd-44ce-973b-40edef508bb1","uuid":"021e42c0-c320-4826-a5cd-89daf63e64ad","timestamp":"2026-10-04T08:03:28.557Z","request_id":"req_011Cfgr8VadxgtT4K13zquPx"}
